This is something I've wondered about - is there no way to get rid of vertical or horizontal grid lines and keep also the axis labels and  tickmarks? It is often unnecessary to have lines in both directions, for example, with bar graphs, or when one of the axes is categorical. I also think that grid lines can carry misleading implications. For example, imagine you have an x axis with qualitative categories like "small", "medium", and "large". Vertical grid lines might make it seem like the data is quantitative and continuous, when it isn't.

For personal data exploration, I don't think it's a problem to always have grid lines, but for polished public presentation, it would be nice to be able to get rid of them.

-Winston

